{
 "how": "X's placed parlays: what X Parlays shows, read only, on the site owner's devices (admin only: the admin link, #owner=<his Odds API key>, makes a browser his; no one else's page has the tab or reads this file, which stays public all the same). Claude keeps this file from the slips the owner sends in chat; the page only reads it, on every load of the owner's browser, so a change here is what his devices see on their next load. A parlay is id (any name not used before), week, stake, price (the American odds it was placed at), payout (what it pays, stake included), note (optional) and legs. A leg needs: game (an index into games below), player (spelled as ESPN spells him), team, stat, line, side (over or under), and main (true for a book main line like 43.5, false for a 'N+' threshold). Stats: passing_yards, passing_tds, passing_interceptions, attempts, completions, carries, rushing_yards, receptions, receiving_yards, targets, scrim_yards, any_td, fg_made, fg_att, kick_pts, and ml or ats for a whole-game bet, total for the game's points. A whole-game bet takes line 0 (the spread for ats), team set to the side you are on, and player set to whatever you want it called; a total takes the line and side over or under. A line the book moved before X placed the bet is written as the line X took. A parlay X has cleared (settled, and no longer wanted on the page) stays here as history with \"cleared\": true and is not drawn. A finished one clears itself: the betting job marks it cleared (cleared_by auto, cleared_on the date) two Eastern days after its last game, once every game has a final in games.csv (liveparlays/tools/autoclear.py), so it shows in full on its game day and the next day. updated is when this file last changed what X Parlays shows.",
